# semgrep ignore rules for this repository.
#
# Each line excludes a file or directory from all Semgrep scanning using
# gitignore-style path patterns. For rule-specific suppression within a
# file, use an inline nosemgrep annotation (// nosemgrep: rule-id for
# TypeScript/JavaScript; # nosemgrep: rule-id for Python/shell). Add a
# "# Suppresses:" line above each entry to document the targeted rule.
#
#   path/to/file                          # exclude entire file from scanning

# install.sh: curl pipe to bash is the officially documented Bun installation
# method. The invocation enforces --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2, which is the
# maximum TLS control available at this call site. bun.sh does not publish a
# SHA-256 checksum for the installer script, making download-then-verify
# unavailable; a download-to-temp-file approach without checksum would be
# functionally equivalent and is therefore not a meaningful mitigation.
# Suppresses: bash.curl.security.curl-pipe-bash.curl-pipe-bash
install.sh

# frontmatter.ts: the dynamic RegExp in extractFrontmatterField uses escapeRegex
# to sanitise the field argument before interpolation. The field value is always a
# hardcoded string literal at every call site ("id", "status", "updated_at").
# Per-rule suppression is handled by the inline nosemgrep annotation in the file.
